## Upgrading projects from vTODO: {version-previous} to vTODO: {version-release}

In the project's **package.json** file, identify all SPFx vTODO: {version-previous} packages. For each SPFx package:

1. Uninstall the existing vTODO: {version-previous} package:

    ```console
    npm uninstall @microsoft/{spfx-package-name}@TODO: {version-previous}
    ```

1. Install the refreshed vTODO: {version-release} package:

    ```console
    npm install @microsoft/{spfx-package-name}@TODO: {version-release} --save --save-exact
    ```

[!INCLUDE [spfx-release-upgrade-warning](../../includes/snippets/spfx-release-upgrade-warning.md)]

> [!TIP]
> To generate an upgrade report for this project, run the following command from the project root:
>
> ```console
> npx -p @pnp/cli-microsoft365@latest m365 spfx project upgrade --toVersion TODO: {version-release} --output md
> ```
>
> This command generates an upgrade report; it doesn't modify project files. Review and apply the reported changes, preserving your solution's custom code and configuration.

